<title>USA: Former Sprint chairman Henson dead at 71.</title>
<headline>Former Sprint chairman Henson dead at 71.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Paul Henson, who spent nearly three decades leading Kansas City-based United Telecommunications into the giant communications company now known as Sprint Corp, died April 12 in a Palm Springs, Calif., hospital, the company said.</p>
<p>Henson, 71, arrived in Kansas City in 1959 at what was then United Utilities. The company's annual revenues were $38.2 million. He became United's president in 1964 and chairman in 1966. He continued as chairman until retiring in 1990, when the company's annual revenues were nearly $8 billion.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
